    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 973 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tailapa-ii">Tailapa II</a>, who overthrew the Rashtrakutas and claimed descent from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badami">Badami</a>.</li><li>Its kings ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basavakalyan">Kalyani</a> and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola Empire</a> for two centuries over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raichur">Raichur</a> doab and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vengi">Vengi</a>.</li><li>Its courts produced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitakshara">Mitakshara</a>, rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a> literature and an ornate temple style that inspired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysalas</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/someshvara-i">Someshvara I</a>, stricken by incurable illness in 1068, ended his life by drowning in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tungabhadra-river">Tungabhadra</a> river, a death recorded by the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bilhana">Bilhana</a> and in inscriptions.</p></aside>
    </section>

