ola-empire">Chola</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajadhiraja-chola">Rajadhiraja I</a> is killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-koppam">Battle of Koppam</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1076</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramaditya-vi">Vikramaditya VI</a> takes the throne and begins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-vikrama-era">Chalukya-Vikrama era</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1129</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/someshvara-iii">Someshvara III</a> compiles the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manasollasa">Manasollasa</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1162</span><span class="rf-text">The Kalachuri <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijjala-ii">Bijjala II</a> takes royal titles at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basavakalyan">Kalyani</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 1189</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/someshvara-iv">Someshvara IV</a> disappears; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seuna-yadava-dynasty">Yadavas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysalas</a> divide the empire</span></li></ol>
